+From e34b5dd497badd9d63570c6a7ca9d75ec19754c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:03:32 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH 38/83] contrib/cairo 1.16.0 + libc pthread_cleanup_push/pop
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+cairo 1.16.0 cross-built against pixman/freetype/fontconfig/libpng + the X
+stack (xlib + xlib-xrender surfaces; PS/PDF/SVG/GL/xcb/script disabled).
+Builds SUBDIRS=src only (test/pdiff.h `typedef int bool` is rejected by
+gcc16's C23).  pthread forced to -lpthread (substrate gcc has no -pthread
+flag).
+
+cairo's pthread feature probe also requires pthread_cleanup_push/
+pthread_cleanup_pop, which substrate's <pthread.h> lacked.  Add them as
+scope macros: push opens a block recording (routine,arg), pop(execute)
+closes it and runs routine(arg) when execute!=0 — the standard run-on-pop
+behaviour cairo/ksh/etc. rely on.  Cancellation-triggered cleanup isn't
+delivered (substrate has no pthread-cancel runtime), matching current
+support.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
