+build-rootfs.sh bakes rootfs.img entirely in userspace (mke2fs + debugfs;
+no loopback mount, and the setuid/owner=root bits are set INSIDE the image
+via debugfs `sif`, not on the host), and build.sh's body invokes no sudo or
+root checks.  The only step that writes outside the source tree is the
+stage-1 toolchain install into $STAGE1_PREFIX (default /opt/substrate).
+
+Correct the build.sh / AGENTS.md / README.md guidance: invoke `./build.sh`
+without sudo, and note that the prefix is the only thing that might need
+write access — make it user-owned once, or set STAGE1_PREFIX to a user-owned
+path, after which every build (images included) runs unprivileged.
